<Layout title="Privacy and local browser storage | CleanCare" description="How CleanCare handles the private self-check, locally saved toolkit progress, third-party images and external source links."><section class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy in plain language</p><h1>Your choices stay yours.</h1><div class="prose"><h2>Private self-check</h2><p>The self-check answers remain in the page’s memory. CleanCare does not save or receive them. Reloading the page or clearing the self-check removes the answers.</p><h2>Starter toolkit</h2><p>Your checked stages and selected country are stored in this browser using local storage. They are not sent to CleanCare. Reset progress clears checked stages; you can change the country or clear site data using your browser settings.</p><h2>No added analytics or mailing list</h2><p>CleanCare currently has no site-installed analytics tracker, advertising tracker, newsletter subscription or account system. The hosting provider and third-party services may still process requests under their own policies.</p><h2>Fonts, images and external sources</h2><p>The site loads a Google font and some publisher, video and brand images from third-party servers. Loading these resources sends a normal web request to those services. Visiting an external article, product page or social post takes you to another provider with its own privacy practices; some sources require sign-in.</p><h2>Contact and corrections</h2><p>If you choose to email CleanCare, your email provider handles delivery and your message is received by the project administrator. Please do not send personal medical records or sensitive health details. <a href={url('about/#corrections')}>Contact and corrections →</a></p></div></section></Layout>
